WEBVTT

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.930
Hey! What are you doing over here?

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.010
Practicing.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.010
Really? "Practicing" is it?

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:17.970
Semimaru.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.980
Well, I can relate to that.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.560
Watching her struggle gets annoying,
so you can't resist the urge to help.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.560
You're a nice guy, Ango.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.030
By the way, is that white hair
a fashion statement?

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.450
It's really cool,
you're like a musician or something.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.460
I'm impressed you handled that
like an adult, Semimaru.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.580
When I touched his shoulder,
all I felt was solid muscle.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.420
Taking a punch from him would hurt.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.750
Is that why?

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.960
Anyway, this is all Natsu's fault.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:57.260
She always gets instantly attached
to any guy who's nice to her.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:01.060
I knew from the beginning
that's exactly the type of girl she was.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.480
What's that look for, Arashi?

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.190
Wipe that smirk off your face.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.940
Don't mind me.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.270
I see how it is.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.570
What do you mean by that? Quit laughing.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.330
GRAIN IN EAR

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.960
Hi there, Ryo.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.880
Wow, so you're left-handed?

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.460
I think lefties are so cool.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:56.960
Catch you later.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.390
Oh, that's right.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:05.260
Do you mind telling me your birthday, Ryo?

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:06.390
And Ango's too.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.730
Our group usually has
casual surprise parties.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.560
Our birthdays?

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.020
Apparently, I was born sometime in August.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.860
Same for Ango.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.320
So, you're a Leo? Or maybe a Virgo?

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:22.950
Good to know. Thanks.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.620
<i>Everything is going swimmingly so far.</i>

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.880
Well, you know, I'm not interested
in just anybody either.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:40.840
What's wrong?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.180
Hey, Ango.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.930
Did anyone ever tell you
when our birthdays are?

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.010
I don't know the dates.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:53.020
Whenever summer came to an end,
we all just grew one year older together.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.190
That reminds me.

00:03:56.770 --> 00:04:00.070
I've noticed Scorpius sinking in the west
and Orion rising in the east.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.820
That means it's autumn now.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:06.240
So at some point, we all turned 18
without even knowing it.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.250
<i>The selection test happened when I was 17.</i>

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:14.370
<i>Up until then, that test was
the only goal that I strove for.</i>

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.830
<i>Somehow I passed it,</i>

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.000
<i>but all I've accomplished since then
was turn 18.</i>

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.710
<i>Shigeru is still 17, though.</i>

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.060
Is that Arashi?
He never seems to stop swimming.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.310
That's because he enjoys it.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.940
Plus he can go diving for things.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:39.730
He uses whatever he finds
to build chairs or other useful things.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.370
You're good at holding your breath.
Are you a swimmer too?

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.290
More or less.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.040
Were you ever in a competition?

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.420
No, nothing like that.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.380
It was just part of how I got exercise.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:02.840
I was always the fastest.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.550
I'm pretty fast myself, actually.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:07.840
Once your arm heals,
we should have a race.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.220
Does the ship still remain stuck
even when the tide is at its peak?

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:15.390
The bottom of the ship is firmly stuck
between some rocks.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:19.190
Every day, we work on scraping away
some of the rock,

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.570
so we'll eventually be able to
break the ship free.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.900
What the hell is that?

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:26.280
A bathtub?

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.320
Ango helped me bring it up here.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.450
We should put it on the ship.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.200
Could we use it if we cleaned it up?

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.710
I was looking for something to store
the crabs and shellfish that we catch.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.000
I also found one of these for you,
Matsuri.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.670
All right! A sponge!

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.380
I'll wash and dry it right now.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:48.430
I also found this little box here.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.890
Wow, is this for real? A toybox?

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.730
And it's in great condition.

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:58.310
-Check out the bracelet.
-There are playing cards.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.440
And a music box.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.330
<i>I know this song.</i>

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.790
<i>I heard it playing back then.</i>

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.090
Oh, what's this song again?
What was it called?

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.710
It's a classical song, right?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:28.630
It's Chopin's "Tristesse."

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.260
Oh, really? You're super smart, Ango.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.850
So you've really become addicted
to beachcombing?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.150
What's that?

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.190
It means you collect things
that wash up on shore.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.650
Depending on the beach, you can
find things from all over the world.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.570
All over the world?

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.870
The sea really does connect everything.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:55.410
The past, the future...

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.450
Even to other people
who live in the present.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.750
<i>And that includes Hana. I just know it.</i>

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.840
Hey, Matsuri?

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.630
I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.010
What happened yesterday?

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:15.260
When I said that I'm not interested
in dating just anybody,

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.270
the truth is,
I said it because I really did think

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.020
that you were okay with any guy.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:25.730
I'm sorry if that made you feel bad.
I shouldn't have been so inconsiderate.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.150
Thank you.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.820
I've never had anybody apologize to me
like that before.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.870
But actually,
you weren't being inconsiderate.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:37.620
To be honest, I put on an act
to make people underestimate me.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:39.700
You want people to underestimate you?

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.120
Because that makes it easier to live,
in some places, anyway.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.500
But now I understand

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:49.960
that's not true of our relationship,
so I don't have to act that way with you.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:54.430
I think I was the one being inconsiderate.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.550
You don’t like being teased, right?

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:58.010
Sorry for taking it too far.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.480
I promise I'll be better about it
from now on.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.770
But tell me if you make any progress
with Ango.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.770
There's nothing between us.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.570
Hey, Natsu. It's time for practice.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:10.570
Wow! He's so assertive!

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:19.040
"In the dawn,
you can see moist splashes of red,

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.620
the flowers of Chengdu,
drooping wet from rain."

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:27.290
Are you Hibari? You finally woke up?

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.460
Why do you know who I am?

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.470
My name is Mansaku Tsunomata.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.590
I'm part of Team Spring, the same as you.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:38.050
Where are the others?

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.060
I don't know.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.600
We all got separated in a big flood.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:44.390
I was saved by people in Team Summer B.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:46.770
They were sailing on a ship.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.900
Really? Then we should go find them.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.940
No. I don't want to.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.240
I left because I didn't
want to stay with them.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.570
Is that so? Well, okay.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.450
I'm getting sleepy.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.950
Then sleep.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.040
Kids like you need to be well-rested.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.460
Just don't forget
to wake up this time, okay?

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.880
"As I thought of the remote utopia,

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:14.260
all I could do was lament
over the blunders in my life."

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:15.680
That about sums it up.

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:23.680
Yes, about here should be good.

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.810
What? What was that just now?

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:39.910
-The rock!
-No way!

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:44.290
If the ship is still stuck at high tide,
we'll cut off some more of the rock.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:48.870
If we can catch a good wind,
the ship should be able to sail again.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:54.170
You boys had gunpowder all this time?

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:55.670
Don't you have any?

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.260
Well, we do.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:04.350
Check it out! The ship is upright!

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.980
Where exactly were you all
trying to sail to before?

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.310
We wanted to learn more
about this new world.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.610
So we were planning to go
from one end of this land to the other,

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:15.780
and maybe even meet with the others.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:20.820
It would be nice to make a map
if anyone had proper surveying skills.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.740
Would you like to set sail again
and continue that journey?

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.240
-Let's do it!
-Totally!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:27.410
I was just starting
to get sick of this place anyway.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.080
We've got to start gathering supplies.

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.590
Like food, water, and firewood.

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:40.720
Are you keeping a record?

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:43.220
What? Oh, well, yes.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:46.890
These plants burn easily,
so they're good for starting a fire.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:50.310
Oh, that's right.
You've always been bad at starting fires.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:54.480
I can only get it to make smoke.
What am I doing wrong, Ango?

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.280
What?

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:00.320
Ango...

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.070
She's not Shigeru.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.620
Is something wrong?

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.960
Corona Borealis oddly stands out
in the night sky.

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:16.340
An oracle once told a man

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:21.470
that he would encounter misfortune
if he married the woman he longed for.

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:28.220
So the man secretly sailed off without her
and left her marooned on an island alone.

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:31.940
Are you saying that letting those two
sail with us would lead to misfortune?

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:35.060
Misfortune? I don't think
that's the right way to put it.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:37.650
It's more like... Well...

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:42.570
Never mind, I think my imagination is
just running wild tonight.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.540
Our test has begun.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:52.540
Yes. That's right, Ango.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.010
CHIMAKI

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.510
Wow! Chimackie made Kumamoto Castle!

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:05.220
I wasn't entirely finished with it yet.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:06.930
I wanted to color it too.

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:09.720
Hopefully,
someone else will find it someday.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:11.180
I see.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:13.020
Is that why you made it?

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:13.980
No.

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:15.730
I did it because I wanted to.

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.310
All right, then.

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:19.650
Now, it's time to set sail again!

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:21.280
Let's go!

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.110
TEAM SUMMER B
TEAM SUMMER A

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:30.790
<i>Our ship slowly set sail.</i>

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:39.420
How are you feeling?

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.380
If you're tired, we can take a break.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.260
Why do you keep asking?

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:45.930
If you want to take a break,
then just do it.

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:48.680
No, I'm used to long trips like this.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.810
But I thought it might be hard
for a lady like you.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:54.850
I can run a full marathon, no problem.

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:58.690
In terms of endurance, I don't think
there's a difference between us.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.770
Muscular differences are
unavoidable, though.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.030
At the facility we were raised in,

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:05.400
boys and girls
were mostly treated equally.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.870
We all had to accomplish the same goals
and take the same test.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:11.620
I see. I apologize.

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:14.620
Fubuki. Ms. Mitsuru.

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:19.500
Now they're a muddy mess.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:22.130
Did you name them
after members of your team?

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:23.340
Yes.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.510
But I came to regret it afterwards.

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:29.800
I'm not entirely sure
what the lifespan of these dogs is.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:35.140
But I think the day will come when
I have to watch them die all over again.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:38.020
I don't think any good can come from
thinking about that.

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:41.320
You might very well end up dying
before they do.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.110
That's true. You make a good point.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:47.360
We all live in the present,
right in this very moment.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.160
There's nothing more to it.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:51.410
We might not have much left ahead of us.

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:53.660
People can die very easily.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:58.170
But the fact you're collecting
and studying the plants of this world

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:02.840
means that you believe we still have
a tomorrow. Isn't that right, Ms. Ayu?

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:11.600
Hey, Taka.

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:16.350
When the full moon comes, I might act
a bit strange, but just leave me be.

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.230
Oh, of course.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:20.980
I realize that ladies have
a lot to deal with.

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.360
That's not what I mean.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.570
I just don't like it
when the moon is watching.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:28.450
Really? So you feel that way too?

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:29.490
What?

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.450
I've had similar thoughts
about the moon before.

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:36.370
That there might be people up there
looking down on us.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.160
What?

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:41.540
If humanity knew
that life on Earth was doomed,

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:44.300
I always thought some
must have fled to space.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:47.210
I like to think they secretly built a base
on the moon

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.430
and there's a bunch of survivors
living there,

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:52.890
watching what happens on Earth
through a giant telescope.

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:54.050
How stupid.

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:56.470
Sorry.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:59.600
I was by myself for a long time
and always had thoughts like this.

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:02.100
That people were alive somewhere

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:04.110
and that I would meet them someday.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:12.280
Taka, the little black one
is getting bullied.

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.820
Darn. Again?

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:15.280
It must have upset them.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.950
I think they're making sure it knows
who the leader is.

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:20.830
Will it be okay?

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:22.960
Yes, they aren't actually biting it
with any force.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:28.050
Ms. Ayu, would you be willing
to adopt that dog?

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:28.960
What?

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.630
That one doesn't seem capable of
fitting into the group.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:35.600
I think it might be best
if it was raised separately as your pet.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:39.350
It's a really nice and friendly pup.

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:40.890
I see.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:42.440
Well, I don’t mind.

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.980
It will definitely keep you warm
on the cold nights.

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:56.370
She's incredibly skilled,
so what's she doing this for?

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:00.580
It's got a living and dining area.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:04.120
Pretty spacious, right?

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.420
The bedrooms are fore and aft.

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.590
Boys are that way, girls the other.

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:09.420
Over here is the toilet and sink.

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:10.510
What's this?

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:11.840
Oh, this room?

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:14.010
We don't know
what it's supposed to be for.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:16.220
So we've been using it for storage.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.430
This must be the bath.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:20.430
The bath?

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:21.560
It's a sauna room.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:22.640
A sauna, you say?

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:26.980
You heat up some rocks
and pour water on them to create steam.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:31.900
<i>These two are very knowledgeable
and have been a big help to us.</i>

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:36.490
<i>Perhaps that's the reason I feel
so excited about going on this journey.</i>

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:41.040
Why exactly are you flying a kite?

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.790
It's visible from very far away, right?

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.170
I thought someone might catch sight of it.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.460
That's a good point.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:49.670
That kite was how we found you.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:50.630
Is that right?

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.130
Awesome!

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.010
Are you okay? You don't get seasick?

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.550
Me? Well, no.

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:00.010
Back when we started,
I did get a little seasick,

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:01.680
but I'm just fine now.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:03.810
I see. That's great.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.390
<i>Why?</i>

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:08.060
<i>I really don't understand
why he's being so nice to me.</i>

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:13.070
Hey, could you tell me
why you're always so nice to me?

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:14.650
What?

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:15.990
"Nice"?

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:21.950
Oh, forget I asked.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:23.580
I'm sorry.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.370
<i>I'm so embarrassed.</i>

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:30.500
<i>I never realized how nerve-racking it is
when someone responds with silence.</i>

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:34.970
<i>I must have caused so many problems
for everyone with my habit of clamming up.</i>

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:39.600
<i>Maybe Ango is just as awkward as I am
when talking with others.</i>

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:42.680
I won!

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:45.230
Damn it!

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:48.150
Does anyone here really think
Old Maid is all that fun?

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:50.860
Who wants to play poker instead?
We can bet with points.

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:53.610
No way!
I just know you're going to rip me off.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.200
A cop shouldn't gamble!

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:59.280
Any idea what else we can play
besides poker?

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.620
-That's not fair!
-I think President is the best.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.290
-Okay, that sounds good.
-I'm down for it! Let's play!

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.920
Come on, hurry up and deal.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:09.880
Okay, let's play.

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:13.880
It's pitch black.

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:16.470
Can't see the ocean or the shore.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:20.340
We survived,
but have nothing to be proud of.

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:22.430
In fact, we even seem pitiful.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:23.760
Why is that?

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:31.440
Weird. I've suddenly got a headache.

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:33.110
Yes. Same here.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.070
It's been a long time since we sailed.
Maybe it's seasickness?

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:39.780
<i>I feel terrible, like I'm going to barf.</i>

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.990
It got really quiet all of a sudden.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:45.040
<i>Charcoal fire and a lack of ventilation.</i>

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.330
<i>That's all it takes
for carbon monoxide poisoning.</i>

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:50.420
<i>A similar incident happened back then too.</i>

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:54.340
<i>Notice it already! The test has started!</i>

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:00.430
Man, I'm feeling dizzy.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.050
If you feel strange, then get out!

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.390
It's carbon monoxide poisoning!

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:07.430
<i>Shigeru!</i>

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:13.060
Everyone out! now! Get outside!

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:14.230
Drag them out.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.360
What the hell happened?

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.950
If you burn charcoal
without proper ventilation,

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:27.910
dangerous levels of carbon monoxide
will build up.

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.080
You didn't have good ventilation.

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:31.870
Why didn't anybody notice?

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:33.500
You all could have died!

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:35.250
It would have been over in an instant.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:36.880
Are you stupid or what?

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.760
Yes, I'm stupid.
I don't know jack shit about all that.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:42.590
I let myself get careless.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:44.470
I appreciate your quick thinking.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:47.010
You should rest for the next few days.

00:19:47.810 --> 00:19:50.560
It's possible you may pass out
even after the fact.

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:52.560
If that happens, it's too late.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:55.770
Oh, thank you so much.

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:58.730
I'm sorry.

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:01.650
Be more attentive.

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:06.070
Be attentive and avoid potential dangers.

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:09.330
That's the only way to survive here.

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:17.090
<i>It must have been tough for our professors
to make sure not everyone died.</i>

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.630
<i>So then, one at a time.</i>

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:28.430
It seems none of us have
any serious symptoms.

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:29.640
That's a relief.

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:32.270
I feel bad about ever mentioning
that stuff about misfortune.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:35.690
It's a good thing
those two came along with us, right?

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:38.610
Yes.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:42.030
Damn! I'm bored out of my skull,
just sitting still for days!

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:44.610
It's okay now, right? We're all healthy.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:47.240
I'm starving!

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:49.080
What?

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:50.910
What are you writing?

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:53.040
Just something to kill time.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.920
IF SOMEONE FINDS THIS,
I HOPE WE MEET SOMEDAY.

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:04.010
I'm surprised.
You're more of a romantic than I thought.

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:05.340
Was that a letter to Hana?

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:07.640
No, it wasn't addressed to anyone.

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:10.430
I just figured it might wash up somewhere.

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:11.720
"Hana"?

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:14.180
That's Arashi's girlfriend.

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:16.100
Apparently, she's part of Team Spring.

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:19.270
I can't believe two lovers ended up
a part of this. It's so magical.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:26.070
-I can't see it.
-I can't see it.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:26.990
Hana...

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:29.700
It shouldn’t come as a surprise.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:33.410
Professor Takashi simply let his daughter
and her boyfriend be in the program

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:34.750
with no strings attached.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:38.670
Just how unfair can this get?

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.460
Was Arashi even a person
worth sending to the future?

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:43.340
Or is he a cheat?

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:45.550
We'll find that out soon enough.

00:21:46.630 --> 00:21:48.260
If he can survive in this world,

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:49.680
then we'll know.

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:53.060
Just forget all about Hana.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:55.270
She's dead now.

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:58.100
And we don't have to tell Arashi
anything about it.

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:02.360
Well, I'll go dive down
and find something useful.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:05.070
I'll get some rocks for the sauna too.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:09.070
Oh, I totally spaced out. The sauna.
We should all use it on Saturday.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:10.160
Yes!

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:13.290
Are you okay, Arashi?

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:14.660
Yes.

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:16.790
I'll take it easy
until I'm properly warmed-up.

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:20.040
Let me help you out.
